    "q": "What about altitude sickness?",
    "a": "The highest point is 4,065 m at the summit, and you sleep at around 3,640 m at Pikey Base Camp. Some trekkers feel mild symptoms such as headache or tiredness at this height. The itinerary gains height gradually, and your guide is trained to watch for signs of altitude sickness. Drink plenty of water, walk at a steady pace and tell your guide if you feel unwell. If symptoms worsen, descending is always the right decision."
